-- Step 40: employees, their pay, their attendance, and the dated statutory tables payroll reads.
-- track: C
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/payroll/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- An employee is paid monthly (basic pay, allowances, fixed deductions) or by the day (a daily
-- wage); each part of their pay is a dated row. Their days for a month come from the attendance
-- file: days worked for a daily employee, unpaid days off for a monthly one. Payroll runs,
-- payslips and journals are Step 41's: nothing here posts anything.
--
-- The statutory tables (salary_tax_slabs, statutory_rates) are copied to every company, like the
-- tax tables of drizzle/0004_tax.sql, with only the figures read in a primary source; a change in
-- the law is a new dated row.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE300 to SE399 (docs/PARALLEL.md):
--   SE320  how an employee is paid does not change once they have pay on record
--   SE321  an employee is linked only to a member of the company
--   SE322  a daily employee has a daily wage; a monthly employee basic pay and allowances

-- ── generated by drizzle-kit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

